  "contract_differences": [
    "Original source UI hardcodes 2020-2025 and caps the displayed top form at 5. Original REST BenchRequest instead requires zoo/universe/period, has top default 20 and bounds 1..500. The migrated form reads the original REST schema; required fields without defaults stay unspecified, while an explicitly selected factor/universe is carried forward. The original result summary still shows at most five rows.",
    "Original Reports scans at most 100 native runs and filters reports with metrics. It provides client-side search, creation-date/status filters and sorting, but no offset or full-directory pagination. The migrated view labels this scope explicitly.",
    "The factor bench operation invokes the same original REST bench_runner.run_bench result contract, not the different AlphaBenchTool top-row result. Compare retains the original compare_alphas result.",
    "Router, i18n, draft keys, chart theme and host errors are scoped locally. Original API runtime, auth, global settings shell, internal server URLs, SSE and live trading writes are not imported. Unknown writes only reconcile signed receipts with GET.",
    "Native dead_examples may contain a category=alive row in a single-factor run. The local Chinese table heading names lower-ranked examples; row badges and all native classification/calculation results stay unchanged.",
    "Native ML trades.csv records execution-event rows using timestamp/code/side/price/qty/reason/pnl/holding_days/holding_bars/return_pct/event. NativeTrades uses the original RunDetail presenter. return_pct is already in percentage units and is formatted without multiplying by 100; no entry/exit pairing is synthesized."
  ],
